-- Fuller Abouts for the first 30 (10 events, 10 groups, 9 businesses), researched from their
-- own pages and other sources and approved by Jesse on the review page on 2026-10-24
-- (https://claude.ai/artifact/SkJhyPEgFMcK4rg17s6Xnz). Laser Dentistry is left out: its site says
-- the practice moved to Becker.

update public.club_events set description = $about$The Sisters of Saint Benedict's Monastery mark the anniversary of Sacred Heart Chapel, finished in 1914 and consecrated in 1943 once the mortgage was paid. It opens Friday at 7 p.m. with Evening Prayer, a procession, candle lighting and incense. Saturday brings Morning Prayer at 8:15 a.m., Eucharist at 11 a.m. and Evening Prayer at 5 p.m., all in the chapel, and the sisters invite everyone to join them.$about$ where id = '66847f53-16b6-4e05-b969-db5c0c1bf9ba';  -- Sacred Heart Chapel Anniversary
update public.club_events set description = $about$Saint John's men's soccer hosts Carleton in an NCAA Division III MIAC game, the Johnnies' last regular-season home match before the conference tournament. It's a matchup near the top of the league: Saint John's comes in 13-2-2 (5-2-1 MIAC) and Carleton 10-4-1 (6-2 MIAC), fourth and third in the standings.$about$ where id = '9380276c-c18a-42a1-8006-b9af45067066';  -- SJU Soccer vs Carleton
update public.club_events set description = $about$A free Halloween morning for families at Trobec's: kids can climb aboard school buses and other big community vehicles and sit in the driver's seat. There's trick-or-treating, a bounce house, free hot dogs grilled by Trobec's staff, photo spots and a coffee truck (coffee for purchase). Costumes encouraged, no registration needed, and kids must come with an adult.$about$ where id = 'a1582885-4218-40d6-abdf-2d604d7fd3ed';  -- Touch A Bus
update public.club_events set description = $about$Kids can wear their Halloween costumes to Coborn's and trick-or-treat through the store aisles. Times vary by store, so check with your local Coborn's before heading over.$about$ where id = '753decd6-afee-4da8-8560-51ee45f1370f';  -- Aisles of Treats Halloween Gathering
update public.club_events set description = $about$Copper Pony hosts plant bingo to raise money for Angel Reins Stable, a rescue for horses whose programs serve veterans, trafficking survivors and others for free. A $30 ticket from angelreinsstable.org covers a cider drink token, a cookie, ten rounds with a card each and a dauber; extra cards are $1, and winners pick plants. It's in the covered pavilion with heaters, so dress warm. Some rescue horses, including one named Bingo, will be there.$about$ where id = 'd1e6e020-dbb4-45c4-bbb8-af2f37259a53';  -- Plant Bingo for Angel Reins
update public.club_events set description = $about$College of Saint Benedict women's swimming and diving opens its home season with a dual meet against Macalester, both NCAA Division III MIAC teams. Macalester brings sophomore diver Ainsley Kashatus, this week's MIAC Diver of the Week and an honorable mention All-American last spring.$about$ where id = '42cf9f39-e3a5-4aff-af59-de463e1714e0';  -- CSB Swim and Dive vs Macalester
update public.club_events set description = $about$Frank Jaymes and the Saints play their first show as a full band at Sal's, a three-hour afternoon set from 3 to 6.$about$ where id = '138ebd2a-881a-4daf-a5d8-cc3950669b0c';  -- Frank Jaymes and the Saints: Live Music
update public.club_events set description = $about$White Peony, St. Joseph's size-inclusive women's boutique, celebrates Halloween with a week of treats and surprises, Sunday through Friday, both in the store and online. The shop hasn't said what the surprises are yet.$about$ where id = '70bf5a73-53d2-457e-a676-e1a65a1f2045';  -- Bootique Week
update public.club_events set description = $about$The weekly Sunday night Mass for CSB and SJU students in the Abbey Church, with music by the SJU Campus Ministry Choir. Confession is offered beforehand, 8:15 to 8:45 p.m. in the Blessed Sacrament Chapel on the east side of the church. Anyone who wants to sing can join choir rehearsal at 7:45, no audition needed.$about$ where id = 'c579dcd8-30c1-47d7-86ce-5e2182e69479';  -- 9 p.m. Student Mass
update public.club_events set description = $about$The city's Park Board, five resident volunteers who advise the City Council on parks and trails, meets at the Government Center. On the agenda: small fixes at Old Kennedy Park, the dog park group's wishlist and 2027 plans, winter and spring activities, and next year's board membership.$about$ where id = 'e55836a6-1c8e-45d5-958b-83c4d5c7018c';  -- Park Board Meeting
update public.clubs set description = $about$The St. Joseph Parish Quilt Group has met since 1986. Its 14 members hand-quilt on a big frame in Heritage Hall every Monday from 7 a.m. to 1:30 p.m., mid-August through March, with December off. Their quilts are auctioned each Fourth of July in the church during the parish festival, and every dollar goes to the parish. In 2025 the 35 quilts raised $12,850.$about$ where id = '62846f8a-0d16-4803-a36a-eb6989e14e79';  -- Parish Quilt Group
update public.clubs set description = $about$A relaxed evening of knitting, crochet and other yarn projects at Milk & Honey Ciders, 6 to 8 p.m. It's hosted by Yellow Brick Knits, run by knitting teacher Trudy Powell, who also gives one-on-one lessons and leads groups. Bring whatever you're working on and settle in at the cidery.$about$ where id = 'f35de225-31c7-4b42-9f48-65d90bbad23d';  -- Stitch and Sip
update public.clubs set description = $about$John Kuebelbeck Squadron 328 of the Sons of the American Legion meets the first Monday of each month at 7 p.m. at the Legion in downtown St. Joseph. It's for sons and other male descendants of veterans who qualify for the Legion, including those whose veteran has died. Co-commanders are Chad and Brad Phillipp, and the squadron is always looking for new members.$about$ where id = '12fca692-1e72-497a-8997-f1e4ff0f8d82';  -- Sons of the American Legion
update public.clubs set description = $about$A free afternoon of handwork in the barn at the Meyer Farm Project, south of St. Joseph. Bring your spinning, knitting, crocheting, mending or any other handwork and join in, 1 to 5 p.m. on the first Saturday of each month, November through April. The farm is a family barn artist Anne Meyer spent over a decade turning into a shared creative space.$about$ where id = '6752a55b-abf3-425f-8a6f-7cef5b423462';  -- Spinning and Knitting Bee
update public.clubs set description = $about$Resurrection Lutheran's adult Bible study meets Thursday mornings at 9 in the Fireside Room. The group uses the Bible as a lens to look at life. It meets year round, and you are welcome every week or on any Thursday you can make it.$about$ where id = '5c2b182f-32fe-4926-bb6a-b1993d62f6a5';  -- Thursday Bible Study
update public.clubs set description = $about$Books are this group's delight. They meet at Resurrection Lutheran on the first Tuesday of the month from 9:30 a.m. to noon, starting with a chat, a short devotion and treats tied to the current book. Now and then they watch a movie or take a field trip instead. Come whether you've read the book or not.$about$ where id = 'c34bee03-87b2-4689-af60-41924322a3cd';  -- Book Discussion Group
update public.clubs set description = $about$Council 7057 is the Knights of Columbus council for the Church of St. Joseph, about 240 men strong, meeting the second Monday of each month at the parish school. Everyone is welcome at their parish breakfast in Heritage Hall, first Sundays through fall and winter, 8:30 to noon: sausage, eggs, hash browns, pancakes, fruit and caramel rolls. $12 adults, $4 ages 6 to 12, kids 5 and under free.$about$ where id = '9717e374-faf7-4427-87ee-a4b1e25c3c3b';  -- Knights of Columbus 7057
update public.clubs set description = $about$A nonprofit group of women who serve St. Joseph, learn from each other and make friends along the way. Projects include a kids' bike safety day at Klinefelter Park with free helmets, birthday bags for the food shelf, tie-blankets for cancer patients and cards for senior residents. They meet the second Monday of the month at the St. Joseph Fire Hall, and women from any town can join.$about$ where id = 'f7ef66bb-0082-4203-b426-4f49241b0981';  -- St. Joseph Women of Today
update public.clubs set description = $about$The American Legion Auxiliary of Post 328 meets the first Tuesday of the month at 6:30 p.m. at the Legion clubhouse. Each spring it runs the poppy drive, with every dollar going to local veterans and active military, and it serves coffee and rolls after the Memorial Day ceremonies. Family members of qualifying veterans can join; call the Post at (320) 363-8631.$about$ where id = 'e5f7123d-b009-4e46-a9d5-d7fadd43cbfe';  -- Legion Auxiliary Unit 328
update public.clubs set description = $about$Supper or snacks at 6, meeting at 6:30, on the first and third Tuesdays at the Millstream Park shelter. The Lions have run St. Joseph's Fourth of July parade since 1964 and now host the town's Easter party. Weekly brat sales and pull-tabs fund giving back to town, from $5,000 for the food shelf to new radios for the fire department.$about$ where id = '3a17193a-088a-436c-ab59-bba9cb306f3a';  -- St. Joseph Lions Club
update public.places set about = $about$St. Joseph Health and Wellness brings several local businesses and providers together under one roof in a refurbished house just south of downtown, the longtime home of the Newsleaders office. It grew out of a merger of The Perfect Fit and Forever Young Two. Today it offers massage therapy, QNRT, Muscle Activation Techniques with a personal trainer, Brockway Dance Complex, and fitness and wellness rooms for rent, plus a VRBO apartment downstairs.$about$ where id = 'f2f87782-f065-4a9b-b812-45f1bd27757e';  -- St. Joseph Health & Wellness, LLC
update public.places set about = $about$Hi, I'm Amy Hedtke, your local State Farm Agent proudly serving St. Joseph, MN and the surrounding Central Minnesota communities! I opened my State Farm office in 2021, and I'm grateful for the opportunity to help individuals and families protect what matters most with clear guidance and personalized service. My team and I help customers with auto, homeowners, renters, condo and life insurance, and a variety of recreational coverages. We're also proud to support our Spanish-speaking neighbors with the help of our Spanish-speaking account manager.$about$ where id = 'cf3c7388-f4ab-4522-ae1d-3d2a018c69a5';  -- Amy Hedtke - State Farm
update public.places set about = $about$The "roots" of Thomsens Garden Center took hold in the late 1970's. We are proud of the fact that we have grown into one of Minnesota's largest greenhouse and garden centers, and through this we have helped thousands of gardeners make Central Minnesota one of the most beautiful places to live! Ryan and Steph Roder aspire to build upon the great name built by founders Bob and Bonnie Thomsen and former owner Arno Shermock. "We grow what we sell."$about$ where id = 'f97e06d6-8cf9-4a75-9acd-b891ba516509';  -- Thomsen's Garden Center
update public.places set about = $about$Exponential Chiropractic Healing Center is Dr. Brian Koltes's chiropractic clinic on College Avenue, offering chiropractic care, acupuncture and help with back and neck pain and work and auto injuries. Dr. Brian grew up in Albany and has more than 20 years in health care as a massage therapist, nurse and doctor, with earlier practices in Cushing, Wadena and Cold Spring. He specializes in soft tissue work, spinal decompression, shoulder injuries and spine rehab, and he does DOT physicals.$about$ where id = '012f809a-029a-426e-8440-4f55ed50d41e';  -- Exponential Chiropractic Healing Center
update public.places set about = $about$Sheryl Matters runs a home-office massage practice in St. Joseph focused on lymphatic massage and ongoing therapeutic bodywork. She is a licensed massage therapist and certified lymphedema therapist trained in Vodder manual lymphatic drainage and Barnes myofascial release. She works with people dealing with chronic swelling, lipedema, post-surgical recovery and long-term wellness, and can continue lymphedema care after insurance coverage ends.$about$ where id = 'e47c4da2-b44f-44d2-af68-adb8181634b1';  -- Sheryl Matters Massage
update public.places set about = $about$We are a multiple-doctor veterinary practice offering a wide variety of services for all animals, including exotics, birds, reptiles and pocket pets. We have been serving the central Minnesota area since 1951. It is our goal to provide the highest quality standards of care in a warm and friendly environment.$about$ where id = 'c9038816-1498-4bf2-8724-d726040b608c';  -- St. Joseph Veterinary Clinic
update public.places set about = $about$Floral Arts, Inc. has been proudly serving St. Cloud and St. Joseph since 1968. We are family owned and operated serving the greater St. Cloud area. We are committed to offering only the finest floral arrangements and gifts, backed by service that is friendly and prompt. We specialize in sympathy designs.$about$ where id = 'c10adb95-4e83-4b9a-95c5-f96178dad197';  -- Floral Arts Inc.
update public.places set about = $about$CentraCare's St. Joseph Clinic on Elm Street is a primary care clinic for patients of all ages, part of the CentraCare health system based in central Minnesota. It offers family medicine, including family medicine with obstetrics, pediatrics, lab services, diabetes care and integrated behavioral health.$about$ where id = 'c70fd279-04d4-46b0-b605-878a85bdb2fa';  -- CentraCare - St. Joseph Clinic
update public.places set about = $about$Whitby Gift Shop boasts a large variety of items for sale, many handmade by the sisters. You will find candles, tea towels, items for infants, cards for all occasions, jewelry, pottery, religious items, scarves, artwork, and much more. It sits in the Art and Heritage Place at Saint Benedict's Monastery, alongside the Haehn Museum.$about$ where id = 'bc27d1cb-ec01-4a70-a084-9948376f8a2a';  -- Whitby Gift Shop & Gallery
